 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Local Ambient Occlusion for Volume Rendering](4300-local-ambient-occlusion-for-volume-rendering.md)
-Calculates ambient occlusion by integrating opacity over the local vicinity's normal distribution, accelerated by approximating the Transfer Function as piecewise linear segments [4300-local-ambient-occlusion-for-volume-rendering.md]. It assumes CT values follow a normal distribution to estimate occlusion probability, reducing computation from iterating over all CT values to the number of TF segments [4300-local-ambient-occlusion-for-volume-rendering.md]. Choose when high performance is needed for CT data with known statistical distributions [4300-local-ambient-occlusion-for-volume-rendering.md].
