 ### [Local Ambient Occlusion (LAO)](4502-local-ambient-occlusion-lao.md)
-Estimates local occlusion by sampling the volume along random directions around the light vector, weighted by distance [4502-local-ambient-occlusion-lao.md]. It differs from global shadowing methods by approximating indirect illumination through incremental, per-pixel accumulation of visibility samples, allowing dynamic interaction with the volume's internal density structure without precomputed global buffers [4502-local-ambient-occlusion-lao.md]. Choose when a soft, noise-based approximation of ambient occlusion is acceptable and precomputation is undesirable [4502-local-ambient-occlusion-lao.md].
